;; Treeless island start: a 9 x 9 sand islet in open water (surface water, floor 1 below), 50 blocks from the east shore, in water that reaches the plot walls on the other three sides (no bank, no tree: the legs toward the walls are nearer than the east shore and find nothing). The only tree stands on the east shore 35 blocks inland: obtain oak_log with :explore and the :worth a kit that needs wood passes (a bare log is worth a few seconds, less than any crossing) must swim the 50 blocks east (go-to swims) and walk on to the tree, which is felled.
;; Should-succeed: the log is got.
;; A 3 high wall runs round the plot, so the body cannot walk off it.
;; Open sky, so the case needs daylight: at night the body waits for light on the bank and the limit runs out (a roofed plot would make the body "buried" and stair up).
{:defaults
 {:tags [:items :obtain :explore :water :jobs]
  :plot {:height 12 :length 200 :width 64 :floor "stone" :light :sky}
  :body {:at [100.5 0 32.5] :yaw 270 :settle-s 2 :inventory [["iron_axe" 1]] :effects [["resistance" 600 4]]}
  :blocks [[:fill [1 -2 1] [150 -2 62] "stone"] [:fill [1 -1 1] [150 -1 62] "water"] [:fill [0 0 0] [199 2 0] "stone"] [:fill [0 0 63] [199 2 63] "stone"] [:fill [0 0 0] [0 2 63] "stone"] [:fill [199 0 0] [199 2 63] "stone"]
           [:fill [96 -1 28] [104 -1 36] "sand"]
           [:fill [185 0 32] [185 4 32] "oak_log"] [:fill [184 4 31] [186 6 33] "oak_leaves[persistent=true]"]]
  :limit-s 700}
 :cases
 [{:name "only-the-wooded-east-shore-across-the-water-is-swum-to"
   :time :day :time-why :night-light
   :act [[:job (jobs.items.obtain {:item "oak_log" :count 1 :ways #{:gather} :explore true :worth 600})]]
   :expect [{:event {:source :job :kind :completed} :within-s 650 :of-job true}]
   :after [[:item "oak_log" [:>= 1]]]}]}
